{"event_type":"review","id":"ede023d5b0566752931ea9f209697b01b2afa38161778ee85dcdaed8b110650d","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T09:54:36Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/de0eade138647a257da73706308abbae7056a7c9da6423b9dddea06b0a6a70e3","sha256":"de0eade138647a257da73706308abbae7056a7c9da6423b9dddea06b0a6a70e3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/071958170d825b26457a433501018a926186b12c6d08bb1cd3a733d193fe1f58","sha256":"071958170d825b26457a433501018a926186b12c6d08bb1cd3a733d193fe1f58"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b3cb0c4a0de2a95ea13f8c35974008077f9f34efc5e21a304500ddb435b8842b","sha256":"b3cb0c4a0de2a95ea13f8c35974008077f9f34efc5e21a304500ddb435b8842b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b62a0782e69a9afc137e1e9180d6f1c189fbb2cd95699fe19d47460922b27db5","sha256":"b62a0782e69a9afc137e1e9180d6f1c189fbb2cd95699fe19d47460922b27db5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/18c34cc14bc1c477a3a800c983f8a54442efde525ba9579a010d29e1a87f7bb1","sha256":"18c34cc14bc1c477a3a800c983f8a54442efde525ba9579a010d29e1a87f7bb1"}],"attempt_id":"093fa959f7cad477935e02047ab08701c38a73d47cd58c89f30baa9dc06dabb5:0:1","base":"7a9e46b3256ca735f7ec19da4a711b8db5119410","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"18ecacb8086b4c654f36395397dec7e55082fa27","body":"**An empty `rev-list` result produces `ids = ['']` and a misleading refusal.**\n\nFor empty output, `''.trim().split(/\\s+/)` returns `['']`, not `[]`. This happens when `head` is already reachable from `base`. One case is a supplied `originalHead` that is an ancestor of `base` or equal to it.\n\nThen `ids.length` is 1, so the `ids.length ? … : Buffer.alloc(0)` guard at Lines 85-87 never takes the empty branch. `cat-file --batch` receives a blank line and answers `missing`. Line 93 then throws `invalid snapshot object`. The operation fails closed, but the error does not describe the cause. The empty-input guard is effectively dead code.\n\nFilter the empty token. Then the empty-set path works as written, or you can add an explicit refusal with a clear message.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   const ids = (await git(['rev-list', '--objects', '--no-object-names', head, '^' + base]))\n     .toString()\n     .trim()\n     .split(/\\s+/)\n+    .filter(Boolean)\n     .sort();\n```\n</details>","id":"65c723fd1c4efb9326c7f2a0c719ec81070f36c8b30a79c105f9372117498701","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/dev/internal/snapshot.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"An empty `rev-list` result produces `ids = ['']` and a misleading refusal."}],"head":"bade3605d0653a5f28415fc8ffa8d8446be3d370","head_tree":"1393f525755319d0614b0af7f33278d124294c49","input_scope":[{"blob":"18ecacb8086b4c654f36395397dec7e55082fa27","intervals":[[1,159]],"path":"src/ops/dev/internal/snapshot.ts"}],"job_id":"093fa959f7cad477935e02047ab08701c38a73d47cd58c89f30baa9dc06dabb5:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"18ecacb8086b4c654f36395397dec7e55082fa27","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/dev/internal/snapshot.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"18ecacb8086b4c654f36395397dec7e55082fa27","intervals":[[18,18],[66,74],[97,101],[138,141]],"path":"src/ops/dev/internal/snapshot.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"18ecacb8086b4c654f36395397dec7e55082fa27","intervals":[[18,18],[66,74],[97,101],[138,141]],"path":"src/ops/dev/internal/snapshot.ts"}],"scope_digest":"01ca04a14ede90f16a79e9125be2723e01806deb89c3bfd1f696b2d2e9ca41bd","source":{"authenticated":